      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You're welcome! High doses of any supplement should be taken with caution, and I'd suggest consulting a healthcare professional before starting any new regimen, especially if you're taking magnesium in high amounts. However, ginger is known for its anti-inflammatory properties and may help with your symptoms. The American Association of Poison Control Centers recommends the maximum dose of powdered ginger to be 1 ounce (28 grams, or 1 tablespoon) per day for adults (about 2 teaspoons) for health problems. But again, I strongly recommend you speak with a doctor before self-administering any new treatment. For your lighting sensitivity, continued breaks and perhaps an over-the-counter eye drop designed for sensitive eyes might improve the situation. Rest assured, eye drops are generally safe and effective for reducing eye strain. If your sensitivity doesn't ease or any new symptoms arise, see a doctor sooner rather than later. Safe travels through your shift!",
      "source": "target",
